WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.536
-Hey, I'm outside Joe &amp; Pat's
Pizzeria and Restaurant

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.737
in Staten Island.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.038
I'm meeting up
with a good pal of mine to try

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:08.841
what some say is the best slice
in New York City.

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:10.143
Let's check it out.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:19.385
♪♪

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:20.786
Ah.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:22.154
Good to see you, buddy.
-Yeah.

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:24.790
-Wow. Here we are.
-The real King of Staten Island.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.459
-No, no, this --
-That's me.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.127
-That's not true. This is --

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.196
I wanted you to be
in the New York show.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.998
'Cause you're very New York
to me.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.600
-I lived in Staten Island,
you know.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.334
-You did?
-For nine days. South Beach --

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:36.836
-Did you really?
-I swear to God.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.037
-Nine days.
-In the '80s.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:40.940
South Beach, Staten Island.
He knows.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.442
-Hi.
-How's it going?

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:43.409
-Jimmy.
-Casey.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:44.610
-Colin.
-How you doing, Casey?

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.778
-Very nice to meet you, Colin

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:47.413
-Casey, how long
have you worked here?

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:51.083
-I'm actually an owner now, but
I've worked here my whole life.

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:52.818
-Yeah, why you insult him,
say he's working?

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:54.253
He said, "I'm an owner."

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.989
-What am I supposed to --
Assume he's the owner?

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.591
Have you ever
been here before, Colin?

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.792
-No.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:01.394
-This is Joe &amp; Pat's.
This is legendary.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.896
-I know. Legendary.
I've heard of it.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.497
-Joe and Pat
are actually my uncles.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.765
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:08.234
-What's the go-to slice here?

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.835
-Never been here before, right?
-No.

00:01:09.835 --> 00:01:11.671
-I would go with the original.
It's my go-to.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.373
I actually had a few slices
for breakfast.

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.074
-I agree, too.
-All right. The original.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.710
Oh, look at this.
-Whoa! Nice!

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.179
-This is what I'm talking about.
-Let me ask you something.

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:21.380
If I want salt on this,

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.882
you'd probably forgive me
because I'm Irish.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.117
-You want salt?
-Probably when Irish people

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.286
come in here, they don't even
remark, no matter what we do,

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:29.422
'cause they're like, "Eh,
they're Irish. They don't know."

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.257
-Yeah. Irish people
don't really have a cuisine.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.591
-Yeah.
-Everything's boiled.

00:01:32.591 --> 00:01:34.727
-Want any spices or anything?
-They patronize us.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.595
-No, thanks.
I would never insult you.

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:39.899 line:0%
-The salt isn't working.
Oh, okay. I think it is.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.467 line:0%
This is good.
I like thin crust, too.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.269 line:0%
-Yeah, look at this.
-You know what I mean?

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.838 line:0%
-Look at this.
Beautiful thing. Do you fold?

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:46.305
-Yeah, sure. What else
are you gonna do?

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:47.473
-Gotta fold.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:49.208
-Don't forget.
I'm from Brooklyn.

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.542
-Holy moly.

00:01:50.542 --> 00:01:51.844
-You know, you think
you're better than their pizza.

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:56.549
-Holy moly.
That is unbelievable.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:59.485
That is delicious.
-It's pretty amazing.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:00.820
-Have you ever seen people

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.555
try to eat this pizza
with a fork and knife?

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.589
-Yes, I have.

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:04.890
-What do you do
when they do that?

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.927
Just sit there? Suffer silently?
-Yeah. Exactly.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.596
-I always see, like, a mayor...

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:11.497
-Yeah. De Blasio. Of course.

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:12.966
-He came here once,
ate with a fork and a knife.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.533
-Oh, my God!

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:15.868
-The number-one rule.
You gotta --

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.236
-You have to fold.

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:20.305
-You have to just
fold and eat, yeah.

00:02:20.305 --> 00:02:23.142
-Oh.
-Wow! Wow!

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:25.177
-That's amazing.
-That's my reaction.

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:26.913
-It's really amazing.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.981
-I got to see you
the other night.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:31.850
It was a really fun dinner.
I had fun because --

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:34.320
You know, we lost a good friend
of ours, Norm Macdonald.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.155
-Yeah.
-And it was good to get together

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.924
with friends
and just talk about him.

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.391
-Yeah.
-You brought up one of the best

00:02:39.391 --> 00:02:42.862
jokes Norm Macdonald --
I forgot that he ever told.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.430
Do you remember what it was?

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.999
-Yeah, one was where he goes,

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:50.303
"I walked in on my parents
having sex once.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.672
It was the worst
30 minutes of my life."

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:57.243
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.512
-That is one of the best jokes
I've ever heard.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.314
That's a fantastic joke.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.716
You have a brand-new show.
-Yes.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.618
-It's called
"The Last Best Hope.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.353
-Yep.
-What's "The Last Best Hope"?

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:10.255
You just have the answer
to everything?

00:03:10.255 --> 00:03:11.857
-No, it's just because --

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:14.627
this country's obviously,
you know, in shambles,

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:18.230
emotionally and, you know,
the unification's gone.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.632
So Abraham Lincoln said,

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:23.102
"We are," about America,
"the last best hope."

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.570
So I just change it.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.505
I am the last best hope.

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:30.343
-And this is at the Lucille --
-Lortel.

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.678
Lucille Lortel.
-Theatre.

00:03:32.678 --> 00:03:34.980
-Yeah.
-You're very French...

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.016
-[French accent] Well,
I don't know. Lucille Lortel.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.150
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.952
-You yell at me.
-Ah.

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:43.289
-To get tickets,
go to colinquinn.com.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.991
Casey, do we have
that special pie?

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.225
-Yep. Got it ready for you.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:47.793
-I got a special pie for us.

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:49.796
-Whoa!
-Look at this right here.

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.897
That's what I'm talking about.
-That's beautiful.

00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:53.799
-Because -- You know
why I thought it was --

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:55.501
You know why I thought
it was perfect?

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.871
Because Norm used to bring you
out on "Weekend Update."

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.106
-Yes.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.373
-And you brought me out
on "Weekend Update."

00:04:01.373 --> 00:04:03.876
-Yes.
-I'll never forget it, bud.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.211
I love you, man.
-I love you, buddy.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.813
-Colin Quinn, everybody.

00:04:07.813 --> 00:04:10.983
He's doing his show at
the Lucille Lortel Theatre.

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:13.085
And I want to thank Casey.
I want to thank Joe &amp; Pat's

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:14.887
Pizzeria and Restaurant
here in Staten Island.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.689
We'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show."

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.391
Look at that love right there.
-Beautiful.

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.726
-Come on.

